  "body": "We are making two related changes related to packaging and from-source installations in 1.68:\r\n\r\n- Rust: #12595 et al\r\n- Sqlite: #12983\r\n\r\nThese should be transparent to anyone using our docker images or our debian packages. However, packagers and those installing from source need to be aware of the upcoming need for a Rust compiler and for a slightly more modern SQLite version.\r\n\r\nWe expect these changes to be uncontroversial, and have sounded out community packagers directly. Nevertheless, when we announce this (in Matrix channels, in a blog post, and maybe in a tweet?) we should call out these changes so that people are given fair warning.\r\n\r\n- [x] Mention in [Synapse announcements room](https://matrix.to/#/!iyIlInqJyxXrRmRHFx:matrix.org/$7sdzd_KII1p3kB_0zT_HG1eYMRX4Nm-9ruyM9Di12AM?via=matrix.org&via=privacytools.io&via=tchncs.de)\r\n- [x] Mention in 1.67 blog post https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix.org/pull/1441",
